From jadhavpr at vcu.edu  Thu Aug  5 16:03:52 2004
From: jadhavpr at vcu.edu (Pravin)
Date: Thu, 05 Aug 2004 12:03:52 -0400
Subject: Re: graph
In-Reply-To: <BAY1-F30tAig3A6EMRP0000562b@hotmail.com>
References: <BAY1-F30tAig3A6EMRP0000562b@hotmail.com>
Message-ID: <04C15615C183B043A3D804C5B989844B076D1C0C@CDSX08.cder.fda.gov>

Try ?xyplot
Here is my way of doing it.I am sure there is a simpler way than this.

###Format the dataset as follows so that you can specify stratification--I
did it manually
test<-data.frame(YEAR=rep(c(1999,2000,2001,2002),2),DV=c(100,150,110,125,50,
100,55,110),SEX=rep(c("MASCULINE","FEMININE"),each=4))

xyplot(DV~YEAR,data=test,
                ##If you don't need overlaid plot delete the following line
and change the model to DV~YEAR|SEX
        groups=SEX,panel=panel.superpose,
                ##Little beautification of the plot
        type="b", lwd=3,lty=c(1,2),pch=c(15,16),cex=1.25,col=1,
        xlab="YEAR", ylab="Number of events"
        )

Thanks,

Pravin

Pravin Jadhav

