Subject: Re: Editing a barplot
Message-ID: <F5F45B096739D311896F0008C7916A700E9AE69F@groexmbcr18.pfizer.com>

  David,

You can use the mtext function to make your axis title. Just leave the ylab
argument to barplot blank (see below). You can modify the arguments to mtext
to make the y-axis label as large as you want. Good luck.

my.mtrx<-matrix(c(18,4,14,10,0,0),2,3)
barplot(my.mtrx,names=c("Placebo","Treatment",""),ylim=c(0,25),
col=c(8,4),ylab="",angle=c(45,135),density=c(30,30))
mtext("Number of Subjects",side = 2, outer = T, cex = 2.2, line = -2)

Steve

