References: <OF86A4DA75.E59925B5-ON88256EED.0080151F-88256EED.0083A268@notes.fs.fed.us>
Message-ID: <000001c47fa6$c98c72a0$0700a8c0@Pravin>

Chris,

I will try to rephrase your question. Let me know if I understand your
question correctly. 

Is there a difference in rate of change of forest vegetation disturbance
between polygons at location(1):ownership(1)   versus
location(1):ownership(2)  versus location(2):ownership(1)  versus
location(2):ownership(2)?

If yes, you are looking at location and ownership as a covariate on slope.
(Pinheiro and Bates in Mixed Effects Modeling in S and S-Plus; page# 365- )
You can test effect of these covariates on intercept as well. But somehow
you seem not be interested in that. 

Just a preliminary observation (I don't have details), your stratification
was done after the first sample was taken. Your current structural model
does not take that design feature into account. I think, it might be
important in testing the effect of ownership as location was the same
anyway.

I hope it helps.

Thanks,
 
Pravin
 
Pravin Jadhav

