Mr. Osburn,

In a recent colleague review of a paper regarding the Durango shutdown you
asked for additional information on the smoothing factor or alpha as
referenced by Cleveland (1994).  The standard reference that I use for
Loess is Cleveland, W.S., and Devlin, S.J., (1988) Locally-weighted
Regression: An Approach to Regression Analysis by Local Fitting. J. Am.
Statist. Assoc., Vol. 83, pp 596-610.   In this there is no mention of a
smoothing factor and I want to avoid confusion (As you know Cleveland was
the world's worst for changing terms--witness the confusion between LOWESS
and LOESS).  No one in my office or the regional office has a copy of this,
and so I would need to get a copy on interlibrary loan.  This would take a
